# s5_per_layer: model converted, encrypted and run one sub-model at a time. Phase B, free.
#
# position   build refused the earlier order: s5_embed_chunk (paid, +2.6%) first, then per-layer driver and
#            streaming loader (+0.9% vs 4.9% wall spread, free); rule 6 forbids free after paid.
#            embed_chunk_cpu moves last.
# levers     the five of s4_onnx_and_spill; the driver is the only difference. Transcript expected
#            s4's 1495 rounds: x0_per_layer_base bytes=11,228,688,384 rounds=1495 = s0_default.
# object     rank 1 at s4's peak: serialized ONNX protobuf and plaintext float32 weights at one instant
#            (whole-model conversion). off-path-runs/s6_conversion_phase/: three releases of 433 MB in that
#            phase, peak unchanged. This step removes the phase.
# expected   ~-30%, 1.5 to 1.6 GB vs 2,289,520 kB.
SHAFT_SCRIPT=$BASE/bert_perlayer_cpu.py
SHAFT_LEVERS=plaintext_free_cpu,triple_share_free_cpu,trace_nograd_cpu,onnx_single_file_export_cpu,encrypt_spill_cpu
